    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0396" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-10T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2542. For Whitehouse<anchor n="89" xml:id="d313-f1"/> from Miles.<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d313-f2"/></p>
                <p>Referring your 2744, June 24, 1 p.m. Consul General at Omsk states that the
                    French General Janin, commander of the Czechs, refuses consent to permit Czech
                    troops to fight way out as suggested. He states Czech troops must be evacuated
                    by sea. Foreign Office at Omsk informs Harris that when the Czechs are removed
                    the Omsk Government must look to America and Japan to supply troops to guard
                    railways. It is understood Japan is favorable to this proposal.</p>
                <p>Stevens cables he would like to be advised whether Czechs are to leave or not and
                    states that unless they are replaced by Allied troops we will have to withdraw
                    American Engineers to [<hi rendition="#italic">from?</hi>] west of Lake
                    Baikal.</p>
                <p>Before referring this to the President I would be grateful to know if you have
                    any further information or suggestion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
